19:T5f0,## 1. Requirements

- Users belong to **groups**; anyone can **add an expense** they paid for.
- An expense splits among participants **equally**, by **exact amounts**, or by **percentage**.
- Track a running **balance**, who owes whom and how much.
- Bonus: **simplify debts** (if A owes B and B owes C, net it out).

## 2. The classes

`User`, `Group`, `Expense`, and a `BalanceSheet` that holds the net owed amounts. A `Group` **composes** its expenses (delete the group, the expenses go) and **aggregates** its members (users live independently).

## 3. The key pattern: Strategy for splitting

Splitting varies, equal, exact, percent, so it's a textbook **Strategy**. `SplitStrategy.split(amount, participants)` returns each person's share; `EqualSplit`, `ExactSplit`, `PercentSplit` implement it. Adding "split by shares" later is one new class, no edits.

```
List<Money> shares = expense.strategy.split(amount, participants);
```

## 4. Tracking balances

The `BalanceSheet` keeps a map like `owes[debtor][creditor] = amount`. When an expense is added, for each participant's share, record that they owe the payer that much (and net against anything the payer already owed them, so balances stay minimal).

## 5. The hard bonus: simplify debts

Reducing a web of IOUs to the fewest transactions is a **graph problem**, compute each person's *net* balance, then match the biggest creditor with the biggest debtor repeatedly (a greedy heap). Mention it: it's the part that separates a good answer from a great one.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-case-studies","activeLesson":"splitwise"}],["$","$L18","splitwise",{"lesson":{"id":"splitwise","patternId":"lld-case-studies","title":"Design Splitwise","kind":"case-study","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Group expense sharing: add an expense, split it (equally / exact / by %), and track who owes whom, then simplify the debts.","companies":["Amazon","Splitwise","Uber","Razorpay"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Model the domain","code":["interface SplitStrategy { List<Money> split(Money amt, int n); }","class EqualSplit implements SplitStrategy { ... }   // + Exact, Percent","","class Group { List<User> members; List<Expense> expenses; }","class Expense { Money amount; User paidBy; SplitStrategy how; }"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":4,"narration":"A Group aggregates its Users (members) and composes its Expenses. Users exist on their own; expenses belong to the group.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"user","name":"User","fields":["- name","- balance"],"x":0,"y":0.2},{"id":"group","name":"Group","fields":["- members","- expenses"],"methods":["+ addExpense()"],"x":1.1,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"exp","name":"Expense","fields":["- amount","- paidBy"],"x":2.4,"y":0.2},{"id":"split","name":"SplitStrategy","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ split(amt, n)"],"x":0,"y":1.55,"tint":"accent2"},{"id":"equal","name":"EqualSplit","methods":["+ split()"],"x":1.2,"y":1.55},{"id":"sheet","name":"BalanceSheet","fields":["- owes: Map"],"methods":["+ settle()"],"x":2.4,"y":1.55}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"group","to":"user","kind":"aggregate","label":"members","toMult":"*"},{"id":"r2","from":"group","to":"exp","kind":"compose","label":"expenses","toMult":"*"},{"id":"r3","from":"exp","to":"split","kind":"aggregate","label":"how"},{"id":"r4","from":"equal","to":"split","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r5","from":"exp","to":"user","kind":"assoc","label":"paidBy"}],"shownClassIds":["user","group","exp"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r5"],"activeIds":["group"]},"vars":[["Group","members + expenses"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"Splitting varies three ways, so it's a Strategy: each Expense holds a SplitStrategy that turns an amount into per-person shares.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["user","group","exp","split","equal"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r5","r3","r4"],"activeIds":["split","equal"]},"vars":[["Strategy","Equal / Exact / Percent"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"A BalanceSheet holds the net \"who owes whom\" map. Six classes, one Strategy, every requirement placed. Now trace adding an expense.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["user","group","exp","split","equal","sheet"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r5","r3","r4"],"activeIds":["sheet"]},"vars":[["BalanceSheet","owes[debtor][creditor]"]]}]},{"label":"Flow: add an expense","code":["void addExpense(Money amt, SplitStrategy how, List<User> who) {","    List<Money> shares = how.split(amt, who.size());","    for (each participant) sheet.record(participant owes payer share);","}"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"A pays a $60 dinner bill for A, B, C and adds it to the Group as an EQUAL split.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"u","label":"User","kind":"actor"},{"id":"g","label":"Group","tint":"accent"},{"id":"s","label":"EqualSplit","tint":"accent2"},{"id":"b","label":"BalanceSheet"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"u","to":"g","label":"addExpense($60, EQUAL, [A,B,C])","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"g","to":"s","label":"split($60, 3)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m3","from":"s","to":"g","label":"[20, 20, 20]","kind":"return"},{"id":"m4","from":"g","to":"b","label":"B owes A 20, C owes A 20","kind":"call"},{"id":"m5","from":"g","to":"u","label":"done","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"The Group delegates the maths to the split strategy: EqualSplit divides $60 three ways → [20, 20, 20]. (PercentSplit or ExactSplit would compute differently, same call site.)","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["EqualSplit","$$60 / 3 = $20 each"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"A paid, so B and C each owe A $20. The Group records that in the BalanceSheet, netting against any existing balances.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["B owes A","$$20"],["C owes A","$$20"]]},{"view":"sequence","narration":"Done. The balances are now consistent and queryable. Swap in ExactSplit/PercentSplit with zero changes here, and layer \"simplify debts\" on top of the BalanceSheet. Clean and extensible.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":5,"activeIndex":4},"vars":[["extend","new split = 1 class ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
